                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.34/188a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-12-09T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 9,
                                1924—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>77. The <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi> this morning carries despatch
                    from Buenos Aires, dated December 8, stating that the Naval Committee of the
                    Brazilian Chamber of Deputies adopted a resolution recommending the construction
                    of 12 warships. The resolution provides for 2 cruisers of approximately 10,000
                    tons each, 4 destroyers of 1,440 tons each, 1 destroyer of 1$800 tons and 5
                    submarines of between 1,300 and 1,500 tons each. The report adds that further
                    aviation development is also recommended. Please cable facts.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
